  <section id="product" aria-labelledby="delays-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Three Delays Model · Thaddeus &amp; Maine, 1994</p>
    <h2 id="delays-heading" class="display-heading">Every maternal death traces to a delay.<br>Sangini works on all three.</h2>
    <div class="delays-grid">
      <article class="delay-card"><div class="delay-badge">1</div><p class="delay-label">Delay 1</p><h3 class="delay-title">Deciding to seek care</h3><p class="delay-desc">Continuous tracking + danger-sign recognition surface risk early.</p></article>
      <article class="delay-card"><div class="delay-badge">2</div><p class="delay-label">Delay 2</p><h3 class="delay-title">Reaching a facility</h3><p class="delay-desc">Coordinated, structured referral shortens the path to care.</p></article>
      <article class="delay-card"><div class="delay-badge">3</div><p class="delay-label">Delay 3</p><h3 class="delay-title">Receiving appropriate care</h3><p class="delay-desc">The patient’s history arrives with her, so care doesn’t start from zero.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</section>

<section id="about" class="about"><div class="wrap about-grid">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">About Us</p>
<h2>Built for the women who carry the system.</h2>
<p>Sangini is a field health system for Nepal’s 52,000+ Female Community Health Volunteers. It turns a spoken visit into a structured record that follows the patient from the village to the health facility, even without internet access.</p>
<p>We presented Sangini at TMSoN 2026, the National Telemedicine &amp; Digital Health Conference. It is in pre-pilot development, and we are looking for NGOs and health programmes to co-develop a pilot.</p>
</div>
<div class="about-list">
<div class="about-item"><h3>Voice first</h3><p>FCHVs speak naturally. Sangini records the visit, so there is no extra form to fill in.</p></div>
<div class="about-item"><h3>Works offline</h3><p>Records stay on the device and sync when a connection returns.</p></div>
<div class="about-item"><h3>Continuity of care</h3><p>A patient’s history travels with her across visits and providers.</p></div>
</div>
</div></section>

